          "input": "const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /tmp/llame-issue-542.md\\n+## Outcome\\n+\\n+Let one owner manage and use multiple independently identified Knowledge Spaces while preserving tenant isolation, live local-file behavior, and portable stable IDs.\\n+\\n+Parent: #39\\n+\\n+## Scope\\n+\\n+- Replace the singleton owner row and bodyless `PUT /api/v1/me/knowledge-space` with owner-scoped create, cursor-paginated list, retrieve, and rename resources under `/api/v1/knowledge-spaces`.\\n+- Keep display names non-unique labels; stable opaque IDs drive ownership, filesystem children, tool selectors, and citations.\\n+- Preserve every existing stable ID and child during migration; assign the migrated singleton the label `Personal`.\\n+- Create the stable-ID child before committing its authority row. Database failure may leave an empty unauthoritative orphan; recovery does not delete filesystem entries.\\n+- Keep Knowledge tool availability separate from owner inventory. Configured and allowlisted tools remain callable with zero spaces and report `knowledge_space_not_configured` when invoked.\\n+- Resolve the owner's current accessible resources at each tool invocation. Added resources can appear later in the same Run; removed access fails on the next check.\\n+- Let `knowledge_search` target one current ID or all current spaces under one shared safety/output budget. Space-scoped failures may return usable results with `complete: false` and bounded call-level warnings; explicit-target, all-target, and global-limit failures remain top-level errors.\\n+- Require every `knowledge_read` call to supply an explicit current Knowledge Space ID.\\n+- Preserve response-time space ID/name, relative path, and exact-byte hash in persisted results; compacted incomplete searches remain marked `incomplete`.\\n+\\n+## API contract\\n+\\n+- `POST /api/v1/knowledge-spaces` with `{name}`\\n+- `GET /api/v1/knowledge-spaces?limit=&after=` with `{items,nextCursor}`\\n+- `GET /api/v1/knowledge-spaces/:id`\\n+- `PATCH /api/v1/knowledge-spaces/:id` with `{name}`\\n+- No `PUT` or `DELETE`\\n+\\n+The list uses a capability-local opaque `(createdAt, id)` keyset cursor. There is no owner inventory count cap in this iteration. Missing and other-owner item IDs return the same `404`.\\n+\\n+## Acceptance criteria\\n+\\n+- One owner can create, paginate, retrieve, and rename multiple same-named spaces with distinct stable IDs.\\n+- RLS/FORCE-RLS plus explicit owner predicates deny cross-tenant enumeration, lookup, search, and read.\\n+- Existing singleton installations migrate without changing resource IDs or filesystem children.\\n+- Tools remain advertised with zero inventory when configuration and allowlisting permit them, and calls report the empty state safely.\\n+- Later calls in an existing Run observe additions and reject removed access without a Chat binding or Run resource snapshot.\\n+- Unscoped search shares all existing limits across spaces and represents scoped degradation without false completeness.\\n+- Read always requires an explicit stable ID.\\n+- API, storage, tools, replay/compaction, and end-to-end negative tests cover the contract.\\n+\\n+## Boundaries\\n+\\n+- API, storage, and tools only; no Knowledge management UI.\\n+- No user upload/population flow, arbitrary host path, deletion/archive lifecycle, import, replica, fork, synchronization, shared ownership, index, trigram search, or embeddings.\\n+- No generic pagination framework or generic partial-result status in this issue.\\n+\\n+## Implementation stack\\n+\\n+`proposal -> storage/API -> tools -> acceptance`\\n+\\n+The OpenSpec change `support-multiple-knowledge-spaces` is the normative implementation contract.\\n*** Add File: /tmp/llame-issue-kb-availability.md\\n+## Outcome\\n+\\n+Tell the assistant which Knowledge Spaces are currently available, including bounded add/remove/recovery changes between accepted model turns, without conflating resource availability with tool availability.\\n+\\n+Parent: #39\\n+\\n+Blocked by: #542\\n+\\n+## Scope\\n+\\n+- Add a server-authored Knowledge resource-availability context producer on the existing system-prompt/system-reminder injection rail.\\n+- Emit a bounded current inventory or delta with stable IDs and display names; names remain untrusted labels.\\n+- Cover zero inventory, additions, removals, renamed labels, partial availability, and recovery.\\n+- Recompute for each accepted model turn so long-running conversations do not rely on stale resource membership.\\n+- Avoid repeating unchanged state and preserve the context-injection capability's ordering, provenance, neutralization, compaction-epoch, and size contracts.\\n+- Tell the model that callable Knowledge tools can still return a current access failure at invocation time.\\n+\\n+## Acceptance criteria\\n+\\n+- The first relevant turn discloses the bounded current state, including an explicit zero-space state.\\n+- Later changed state produces one deterministic reminder; unchanged state produces none.\\n+- Removed resources are no longer presented as currently available, while historical citations remain historical.\\n+- Client-authored metadata cannot forge the inventory or widen tool authority.\\n+- Resource availability does not alter the immutable tool declaration/allowlist snapshot.\\n+\\n+## Boundaries\\n+\\n+- No Chat bindings or Run-level Knowledge resource snapshot.\\n+- No new list tool.\\n+- No authorization decision from prompt text; every tool call still checks current owner access.\\n*** Add File: /tmp/llame-issue-kb-population.md\\n+## Outcome\\n+\\n+Let ordinary hosted users populate their Knowledge Spaces without operator filesystem access, while preserving the configured-root and stable-ID containment boundary.\\n+\\n+Parent: #39\\n+\\n+Blocked by: #542\\n+\\n+## Design gate\\n+\\n+Choose the smallest safe user-facing ingestion contract before implementation: browser upload, bounded text/Markdown creation, a trusted local-node bridge, or a deliberately limited combination. Do not expose an arbitrary server filesystem path selector.\\n+\\n+## Scope\\n+\\n+- Populate one explicitly owned Knowledge Space selected by stable ID.\\n+- Admit only bounded text/Markdown content and safe Knowledge-relative paths.\\n+- Define create/replace/conflict behavior, request limits, filename normalization, and failure atomicity.\\n+- Enforce ownership in the datastore and containment in the filesystem with negative cross-tenant and traversal tests.\\n+- Make newly written content visible to the existing live search/read tools without requiring an index.\\n+\\n+## Acceptance criteria\\n+\\n+- A non-operator user can add a Markdown file to an owned space and retrieve it through Knowledge tools.\\n+- Guessing another owner's space ID, traversal, absolute paths, symbolic links, non-text content, and oversized input fail closed.\\n+- Failed writes do not expose partial content as a successful file.\\n+- The design states how later local-node import/synchronization can preserve stable resource identity.\\n+\\n+## Boundaries\\n+\\n+- Not #212's agent-authored one-file Git/CAS write contract.\\n+- Not #547's replica/import/fork protocol.\\n+- No arbitrary server path, directory mount, bulk sync, index, or embeddings in the first slice.\\n*** Add File: /tmp/llame-issue-pagination.md\\n+## Outcome\\n+\\n+Standardize growing REST collections on one reusable opaque keyset-pagination contract after the Knowledge-local cursor proves the shape.\\n+\\n+Blocked by: #542\\n+\\n+## Scope\\n+\\n+- Extract the minimal cursor encode/decode, validation, limit, ordering, and response conventions proven by Knowledge Spaces.\\n+- Migrate owner and shared chat-history collection pagination from numeric sequence cursors to the reusable contract without changing tenant visibility.\\n+- Use deterministic keyset ordering with an explicit unique tie-breaker.\\n+- Define malformed/stale cursor behavior, generated OpenAPI/client shapes, and cross-tenant negative coverage.\\n+- Inventory other unpaginated REST collections, but migrate only collections with demonstrated growth or correctness need.\\n+\\n+## Acceptance criteria\\n+\\n+- Knowledge Spaces and selected chat-history collections expose one documented opaque cursor convention.\\n+- Cursors are validated, never treated as authorization, and cannot widen RLS-scoped queries.\\n+- Page traversal is deterministic under equal primary sort values and concurrent inserts.\\n+- Existing clients receive an explicit breaking migration path where response shapes change.\\n+\\n+## Boundaries\\n+\\n+- No framework before #542 provides a second real consumer.\\n+- Exclude SSE run-event replay cursors and MCP provider cursors; their semantics are not REST collection pagination.\\n+- No signing, encryption, cursor version framework, total counts, or universal migration without a concrete need.\\n*** Add File: /tmp/llame-issue-incomplete-tool-results.md\\n+## Outcome\\n+\\n+Standardize how usable-but-incomplete tool results survive execution, persistence, replay, compaction, truncation, and UI without being mistaken for complete success.\\n+\\n+Blocked by: #542\\n+\\n+Related: #294, #309, #544\\n+\\n+## Scope\\n+\\n+- Generalize the minimal Knowledge-search convention introduced by #542: a usable success payload may declare incomplete work and bounded warnings, while compacted observations retain an honest `incomplete` outcome.\\n+- Decide the generic result contract across code-owned and MCP tools without assuming every tool can produce partial work.\\n+- Carry the distinction through runner settlement, durable events, assistant parts, history reconstruction, model replay, compaction ledgers, payload truncation, and browser rendering.\\n+- Define bounded per-call versus per-item warnings and safe omission counts.\\n+- Preserve paired call/result replay and existing terminal error outcomes.\\n+\\n+## Acceptance criteria\\n+\\n+- An incomplete result cannot become indistinguishable from complete success after payload clearing, truncation, reload, retry, or compaction.\\n+- Full success, incomplete success, tool error, timeout, cancellation, unavailability, and terminal settlement remain distinguishable where their semantics differ.\\n+- The model and UI receive bounded recovery guidance without raw internals or untrusted status text.\\n+- Legacy rows and unknown schema versions fail closed under an explicit migration policy.\\n+\\n+## Boundaries\\n+\\n+- #542 ships only the minimal Knowledge-specific `complete: false` payload and compacted `incomplete` marker.\\n+- This issue does not redesign durable side-effect checkpointing or generic run recovery owned by #309.\\n+- This issue does not add indexed Knowledge search owned by #544.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n",
