ble results with `complete: false` plus bounded warnings; if every target fails or a global limit trips, the call fails closed.\\n+- `knowledge_read` requires an explicit `knowledgeSpaceId`, even when the user has only one space.\\n+- Existing single-space installations migrate without changing the current space ID or stable-ID child.\\n+- API and database negative tests cover cross-tenant access, malformed cursors, and zero-inventory behavior.\\n+\\n+## Boundaries\\n+\\n+- No Chat defaults, Run-level Knowledge snapshots, or execution bindings.\\n+- No web management, upload, import, indexing, embeddings, or semantic retrieval work here.\\n+- No delete/archive lifecycle, shared ownership, arbitrary host paths, or automatic cleanup of unauthoritative orphan directories.\\n+\\n+## Follow-ups\\n+\\n+- #550 — assistant-visible current Knowledge resource availability\\n+- #552 — user population without operator filesystem access\\n+- #551 — reusable REST collection cursor convention\\n+- #553 — generic incomplete tool-result semantics\\n+\\n+## Implementation stack\\n+\\n+`proposal -> legacy-writer compatibility -> storage/API -> tools -> incomplete replay -> acceptance -> OpenSpec sync/archive`\\n+\\n+The final `multiple-kb/finalize` layer is a separate PR with no implementation behavior. It applies `openspec-sync-specs` and then `openspec-archive-change`.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n",
